  "findings": [
    "Directory sources store the exact manifest as manifest.json, SHA-256 config/layer blobs under their hex digest, and signatures as signature-1 etc.",
    "Version 1.1 is the reviewed SHA-256-only directory format.",
    "signedBy with GPGKeys and exactReference is supported for the directory transport; default reject and all original Docker release/base rules remain intact.",
    "standalone-sign emits a local OpenPGP image signature; actual policy positive and negative controls use skopeo copy on a tiny valid image; no native tools run locally.",
    "The production input bytes remain bound by the existing hosted artifact, OCI manifest and every blob; the ephemeral key is a test-harness identity, not independent release provenance."
